We are given that a **reflection** takes the vector  
$$
\begin{pmatrix} 5 \\ 0 \end{pmatrix}
$$  
to  
$$
\begin{pmatrix} 4 \\ 3 \end{pmatrix}.
$$  
We are to find where the reflection takes the vector  
$$
\begin{pmatrix} -2 \\ 3 \end{pmatrix}.
$$

---

### Step 1: Understand the reflection

A **r ...[cut]... ^2 = 9 + 1 = 10 $

So:
$$
\text{proj}_{\vec{d}} \vec{v}_2 = \frac{-3}{10} \begin{pmatrix} 3 \\ 1 \end{pmatrix}
= \begin{pmatrix} -\frac{9}{10} \\ -\frac{3}{10} \end{pmatrix}
$$

Now compute the reflection:
$$
R\vec{v}_2 = 2 \cdot \begin{pmatrix} -\frac{9}{10} \\ -\frac{3}{10} \end{pmatrix} - \begin{pmatrix} -2 \\ 3 \end{pmatrix}
= \begin{pmatrix} -\frac{18}{10} \\ -\frac{6}{10} \end{pmatrix} - \begin{pmatrix} -2 \\ 3 \end{pmatrix}
= \begin{pmatrix} -\frac{18}{10} + 2 \\ -\frac{6}{10} - 3 \end{pmatrix}
= \begin{pmatrix} -\frac{18}{10} + \frac{20}{10} \\ -\frac{6}{10} - \frac{30}{10} \end{pmatrix}
= \begin{pmatrix} \frac{2}{10} \\ -\frac{36}{10} \end{pmatrix}
= \begin{pmatrix} \frac{1}{5} \\ -\frac{18}{5} \end{pmatrix}
$$

